Compilation
------------
 In 'bin' directory, you will find pre-compiled executables for
 Windows, SGI/IRIX, IBM/AIX, Linux/i386, etc.

 autozmat.exe   --- MS Windows PE 32-bin Intel 80386 console executable
 autozmat.linux --- ELF 32-bit LSB executable, Intel 80386
 autozmat.irix  --- SGI/IRIX MIPS3
 autozmat.aix   --- IBM/AIX 4.2
 autozmat.dec   --- DEC/Alpha

 If you can find an executable you need to use, skip compilation. 

1. UNIX
 In most UNIX systems, you need just type 'make' at the top directory.

2. MS-DOS
 I was able to compile 'autozmat' with DJGPP, CYGWIN, or EGCS-MINGW32.

 1) Check ATOMTYPE_FLAGS and MY_LIBS in Makefile.dos.
 2) make -f Makefile.dos
 3) 'autozmat.exe' will be installed in dos/bin directory.


Installation
-------------

 Executable 'autozmat' is stand-alone. However, sometimes it needs to read
 library files such as oplsaa parameter files or atomtype hash tables,
 which can be found in 'lib' directory.
 Therefore, it is recommended to install 'autozmat' executable and library
 files in the following way.

1. UNIX

 (a) Compilation
    If you see a binary for your system in bin directory, go to (b).
  Otherwise, compile the source as below. You may have to edit Makefile
  for your needs. On some systems, you may have to set PWD variable
  in Makefile manually.

  % make clean_installed
  % make

 (b) Test
    If you have built autozmat by compilation or have a binary already,
  type 'make test' to try out the program.
  You may not have a 100% succeess on tests. For failed tests, examine
  output files in sample/Scratch directory to see whether they are
  acceptable or have errors.

 (c) Installation
    Type 'make install' to install autozmat.

    [NOTE] If you have to install autozmat manually, proceed as below.
       If you want to install 'autozmat' executable in, e.g., /usr/local/bin,
       install 'lib/boss' and 'lib/opls' (optional) in /usr/local/lib. I.e.,
       The parent directory of 'bin' and 'lib' should be the same.

       % cp bin/autozmat* /usr/local/bin
       % cp -r lib/boss /usr/local/lib
       % cp -r lib/opls /usr/local/lib

2. MS-DOS

 If you want to install 'autozmat' executable in, e.g., C:\bin,
 install 'lib\boss' and 'lib\opls' (optional) in C:\lib.
 The parent directory of 'bin' and 'lib' should be the same.

 C:> mkdir C:\bin
 C:> mkdir C:\lib
 C:> mkdir C:\lib\boss
 C:> mkdir C:\lib\opls

 C:> copy bin\autozmat.exe C:\bin
 C:> copy lib\boss\*.* C:\lib\boss
 C:> copy lib\opls\*.* C:\lib\opls

